CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[except.ctor]/1-3 level-by-level unwinding: destructors of every scope exited on
the way to the catching handler run (innermost first), objects are not destroyed
early when an inner handler matches, and a rethrow from an inner handler unwinds
the enclosing scope before the outer handler.  All three scenarios cross-checked
against g++ and clang++.
